00:12:49.223 --> 00:12:50.063
to a tough problem.

00:12:50.063 --> 00:12:51.403
They did this study with doctors

00:12:51.403 --> 00:12:52.573
who have a kind of like, you know,

00:12:52.573 --> 00:12:55.273
house level medical diagnosis
that's really tricky.

00:12:55.273 --> 00:12:56.153
You're in a positive mood.

00:12:56.153 --> 00:12:57.753
You're more likely to see the problem.

00:12:57.753 --> 00:13:00.013
There's evidence suggesting
that your mood levels

00:13:00.013 --> 00:13:02.243
and your cheerfulness levels at 18

00:13:02.243 --> 00:13:03.913
actually predict how
much you're gonna make

00:13:03.913 --> 00:13:05.550
when you're 30 years old, right?

00:13:05.550 --> 00:13:07.183
And so all of you students out there

00:13:07.183 --> 00:13:08.493
who are making yourselves miserable

00:13:08.493 --> 00:13:10.443
by not sleeping and
worrying about college,

00:13:10.443 --> 00:13:12.443
it turns out the causal
arrow might go the other way.

00:13:12.443 --> 00:13:14.143
Your cheerfulness right now

00:13:14.143 --> 00:13:15.803
might be predicting a whole host of stuff

00:13:15.803 --> 00:13:17.583
that's gonna affect your salary later on.

00:13:17.583 --> 00:13:19.223
And so I think it's a problem.

00:13:19.223 --> 00:13:21.498
I think as a society, we
really have it backwards.

00:13:21.498 --> 00:13:25.089
We actually need to be putting
our oxygen mask on first.

00:13:25.089 --> 00:13:27.213
It doesn't just affect
like, Oh, we feel good.

00:13:27.213 --> 00:13:28.223
That feels nice.

00:13:28.223 --> 00:13:30.346
It affects the bottom line in a deep way.

00:13:31.817 --> 00:13:33.633
- That's, super powerful.

