breath for five minutes.

00:14:50.923 --> 00:14:53.313
You're not gonna lose
that much study time.

00:14:53.313 --> 00:14:54.943
If you take five minutes
to do a meditation.

00:14:54.943 --> 00:14:57.093
And what you'll find is
the act of doing that

00:14:57.093 --> 00:14:58.553
is gonna give you back dividends

00:14:58.553 --> 00:15:00.783
in terms of your attention and so on.

00:15:00.783 --> 00:15:02.306
So one of the things I recommend is like,

00:15:02.306 --> 00:15:03.823
especially in this zoom time,

00:15:03.823 --> 00:15:06.553
when we're all experiencing so
much zoom fatigue right now,

00:15:06.553 --> 00:15:09.173
is in between classes
or in between meetings,

00:15:09.173 --> 00:15:11.883
just a three minute
deep breath meditation,

00:15:11.883 --> 00:15:13.593
where you just breathe in deeply

00:15:13.593 --> 00:15:15.883
into your, ideally
breathe into your stomach.

00:15:15.883 --> 00:15:19.463
So big stomach breath in, and
then a really slow exhale.

00:15:19.463 --> 00:15:21.363
And again, it sounds, you know silly,

00:15:21.363 --> 00:15:22.213
you know people say like, Oh,

00:15:22.213 --> 00:15:23.046
take a deep breath

00:15:23.046 --> 00:15:24.263
when you're trying to be like all,

00:15:24.263 --> 00:15:25.943
you know, worried about you
being stressed and things.

00:15:25.943 --> 00:15:28.223
But scientifically, what happens is that

00:15:28.223 --> 00:15:30.533
that deep breath activates
your vagus nerve.

00:15:30.533 --> 00:15:32.813
And if you're taking a
biology class on Khan Academy,

00:15:32.813 --> 00:15:34.483
you probably know that we have this thing

00:15:34.483 --> 00:15:36.573
called the Sympathetic
nervous system, right?

00:15:36.573 --> 00:15:38.873
That activates, that's our
like, fight or flight system.

00:15:38.873 --> 00:15:39.773
That's like, Oh gosh,

00:15:39.773 --> 00:15:41.503
the tiger is coming or an exam's coming,

00:15:41.503 --> 00:15:42.763
I'm so freaked out.

00:15:42.763 --> 00:15:43.673
Well, you wanna activate

00:15:43.673 --> 00:15:45.043
to decrease that stress

00:15:45.043 --> 00:15:46.582
is your parasympathetic nervous system,

00:15:46.582 --> 00:15:48.073
the other part.

00:15:48.073 --> 00:15:48.906
And you do that

00:15:48.906 --> 00:15:50.603
through activation of
the vagus nerve, right?

00:15:50.603 --> 00:15:51.903
When you're taking those deep breaths,

00:15:51.903 --> 00:15:54.213
there's no tiger that
could be coming to get you.

00:15:54.213 --> 00:15:55.713
And it just signals to your body

00:15:55.713 --> 00:15:58.153
to kind of go back to that distress mode.

00:15:58.153 --> 00:15:59.683
And that takes like three minutes.

00:15:59.683 --> 00:16:00.516
And so, you know,

00:16:00.516 --> 00:16:02.248
that's one quick tip that
you can kind of build in.

00:16:02.248 --> 00:16:05.033
But another one is just like, again,

00:16:05.033 --> 00:16:07.313
it's, it's a broader
more meta issue, right?

00:16:07.313 --> 00:16:08.783
One of the reasons we're so stressed

00:16:08.783 --> 00:16:10.693
is that we're going after the wrong stuff.

00:16:10.693 --> 00:16:12.142
You know, what if everybody on this call

00:16:12.142 --> 00:16:15.297
